      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "A right-angled triangle has legs of length $3\\text{ cm}$ and $4\\text{ cm}$. What is the length of the hypotenuse?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$\\sqrt{7}\\text{ cm}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$25\\text{ cm}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$7\\text{ cm}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$5\\text{ cm}$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "d",
      "explanation": "By Pythagoras' theorem: $c = \\sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 16} = \\sqrt{25} = 5\\text{ cm}$."
